\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.2}{\ignorespaces Comparison of AABB-tree and quadtree search structures for a circular immersed surface. The AABB tree recursively partitions the surface elements and encloses each group within a bounding box, whereas the quadtree recursively partitions the surrounding spatial domain.}}{96}{figure.caption.73}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.3}{\ignorespaces Schematic representation of the ghost-cell treatment near an immersed boundary. The standard approach (a) defines ghost-cell directly near the immerse-boundary, while the modified approach (b) adjusts the positioning of the ghost cells according to the prescribed modeling distance $H_{\mathrm {mod}}$ used for the RANS wall treatment.}}{97}{figure.caption.74}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.4}{\ignorespaces Mask functions used in the penalized Eulerian droplet formulation: (a) solid--fluid mask $\chi $, (b) droplet-direction mask $\chi _d$, and (c) combined penalization indicator $\chi \chi _d$, which restricts the penalization to the overlap between the immersed-solid and incoming-droplet regions. \textcolor {blue}{Adapted from~\cite {lavoieDroplets}}.}}{101}{figure.caption.75}%
